{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffdHHkxoe5STvnLoKinT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The candidate is written and passes the self-check: it loads, its log-probability is finite, it meets the data contract, and the smoke fit gives a finite ELPD-LOO. It fits worse than the current best model, though: about −3001 on the short smoke fit, against −2243 for the best.\n\n**Model: `switch_after_repeat_markov_coin`**\n\n- **Hypothesis:** People judge randomness with a subjective coin that remembers only its last two flips. The chance that the next flip switches sides depends on whether the last two flips were a repeat or a switch. A sequence looks random to the extent this coin finds it probable, so long streaks (repeat after repeat) and strict alternation (switch after switch) both look less random. On top of that, each person has a small habitual lean toward clicking left or right.\n- **Why this idea:** The brief asked for something simpler or riskier. This mechanism was tried once before as `two_flip_memory_subjective_coin`, but it was rejected because its fit didn't converge, so the idea itself was never tested.\n- **Implementation:** It has three shared switch probabilities (first transition, after a repeat, after a switch), each on the logit scale. A strength parameter scales the difference in log-probability between the two sequences, and the personal lean is hierarchical and non-centred, with 400 participant slots.\n\n**What the check didn't cover:**\n- **Convergence:** with a single chain the check can't report R-hat, so whether it passes admission's convergence gate is unknown.\n- **ELPD reliability:** 1.4% of trials had high Pareto k, above the 1.0% tolerance. That may only reflect the 100-draw smoke fit, but admission's full fit could also call it unreliable.\n- **Novelty:** not checked against the other models.\n\nThe model doesn't directly address the critique's finding that people prefer more balanced heads/tails counts at equal switch counts, because it only looks at switches and repeats. If it loses, that is an informative result.\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_0`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":883,"cache_read_input_tokens":72762,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":883,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"209e104b-0c94-41d2-9c19-d165bb6f2408","uuid":"5c4bbb1a-7208-410b-95ed-1ba4751c19f2","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:33:56.900Z","request_id":"req_011CffdHHMuKt4kEL8R61hew"}
